Tycoon 2FA operators added an OAuth device-code variant alongside the credential-relay kit rather than abandoning it, and the Alibaba (US) hosting eSentire saw since about 2026-04-10 joins the previously documented providers instead of replacing them. The lure shows a device code fetched by the operator's backend and has the victim paste it at microsoft.com/devicelogin; the detection signals are eSentire's own (successful deviceCode sign-ins from sources with no prior device-code use, the Microsoft Authentication Broker AppId, node or undici user agents, ResultType 50173 after revocation). eSentire's hardening leads with a Conditional Access block on the device-code flow, and no source says that FIDO2 sign-in defeats device-code phishing.
